        "root_concepts": "[arthropoda]",
        "section": "animal-phylogeny",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Arthropoda - The Most Species-Rich Phylum",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nCUTICLE LAYERS (outside to inside)\n+--------------------------------------------+\n|  Epicuticle     Thin, waxy, waterproof     |\n|                 (wax layer = key land      |\n|                  conquest innovation)      |\n+--------------------------------------------+\n|  Exocuticle     Hardened by quinone        |\n|                 tanning (sclerotization)    |\n+--------------------------------------------+\n|  Endocuticle    Soft, flexible,            |\n|                 laminated chitin-protein   |\n+--------------------------------------------+\n|  Epidermis      Secretes above layers      |\n+--------------------------------------------+"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-ARTHROPODA.md#011",
      "path": [
        "06-ARTHROPODA.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:animal-phylogeny:06-arthropoda, git-history:animal-phylogeny:06-arthropoda]",
        "canonical_path": "animal-phylogeny/06-ARTHROPODA.md",
        "concepts": "[arthropoda]",
        "current_path": "animal-phylogeny/06-ARTHROPODA.md",
        "id": "maxim:animal-phylogeny:arthropoda",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "animal-phylogeny",
        "remap_from": "[]",
